  "configuration_id": "config_021",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_013 (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted) at 0.5420 accuracy. The multiprofile + avgpool + weighted combination is strongly validated across experiments (config_006, 013, 035 all confirm multiprofile >> singleprofile, and avgpool+weighted > other combos). Uncertainty: Whether scgpt is specifically required or whether scvi_n200 (a learned 200-dim RNA representation) can match or exceed it within the same proven architecture. This experiment (config_021: scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted) is a clean single-variable test of the RNA encoder while holding all other settings at their proven-best values. It reduces uncertainty about encoder choice and, if scvi_n200 performs comparably, offers a cheaper alternative for future runs. Expected cost: scvi_n200 is a smaller encoder than scgpt, so I estimate ~2.0–2.5 GPU hours, slightly below config_013's 2.94. This is the best use of experiment 5 because it exploits the strongest architectural direction while probing the single most impactful remaining design variable (RNA encoder quality) before committing remaining budget to further exploitation or alternative image encoders."
}

